The prose samples in this directory are NOT covered by the repository's MIT
licence. They are essays from Project Gutenberg, reproduced under:

    Public domain (works out of copyright)
    https://www.gutenberg.org/policy/permission.html

Project Gutenberg's own Trademark License applies to any redistribution that
carries the "Project Gutenberg" name. To stay clear of it, each essay here has
its frontmatter naming Project Gutenberg as the SOURCE only, and the text body
itself carries no PG boilerplate - the ***START/END*** markers, the header and
license notice, and the footer are stripped by fetch-essays.mjs.

ATTRIBUTION.json lists every essay's author, source volume, Gutenberg eBook id,
and original publication date. The eBook id resolves to
https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/<id> for anyone re-deriving the corpus.

Sibling directories (`human/`, `ai/`) are CC BY-SA 4.0 Wikipedia text with
their own LICENSE. Nothing has changed there. This directory sits alongside
them for the same reason they exist: to give the critics real prose to be
tested against, with provenance a reader can check.

Nothing may be added to this directory except text that is public domain or
under a licence at least as permissive - CC0, CC-BY, or an OSI-approved
equivalent - with provenance recorded the same way. Not contemporary
journalism (except CC-BY-published), not contemporary books, not private
writing, however good a sample it would make. The tests do not need it; the
public repo cannot host it.
